This example only shows the very basics of contract testing and the Pex tool. It might need more refinements for better practice. You should always ensure that your own test suits adequately test your code. If the Pex tests fail, look closely at the messages - this can provide insight into what caused the test failure. The failing test output will usually provide a wealth of information as to the nature of the problem - be sure to examine this closely. And, ensure that you understand how your specific code's behaviour changes with each method you test. Happy Testing Peer!!

